course: dictionary
lesson: 13905
title: Larval: the young stage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Larval is an adjective. It describes things to do with a larva, the young stage of an insect, frog or other animal before it changes into its adult form.
explain: «The larval stage of a butterfly is the caterpillar.» The caterpillar is the young, not-yet-changed form. Later it will change into an adult butterfly, so larval means young and not yet grown up.
explain: Scientists use the phrase «the larval stage» when they talk about a life cycle, the set of changes a living thing goes through from young to adult. Knowing this word helps you follow the story of the cycle.
fact: Larval means to do with a larva.
fact: A larva is the young stage of an insect, frog or other animal, before it changes into its adult form.
fact: «A tadpole is the larval stage of a frog.»
fact: «A caterpillar is the larval stage of a butterfly.»
fact: Larval is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as stage or form.
exercise: «A caterpillar is the larval stage of a butterfly.» What does larval mean? | To do with the wings of a bird | To do with the adult animal, after it has finished changing | To do with living only in water | *To do with the young stage, before an animal changes into its adult form
exercise: «The larval form of a dragonfly lives in the pond for a long time.» Which word tells you the dragonfly is not yet an adult? | long | pond | *larval | dragonfly
exercise: Which animal is in its larval stage? | A bird sitting on its nest | A frog with legs and lungs | *A tadpole | A fully grown butterfly
test:
test: The scientist studied the larval stage of a frog. What does larval mean here? | Dead | Very large | *Young, before the animal changes into its adult form | Adult, fully grown
test: Which phrase means the young stage in a life cycle? | the old stage | the adult stage | the wing stage | *the larval stage
exam: Which sentence uses larval correctly? | Larval means very tall and thin | The larval stage of a cat is a fish | *The larval stage of a butterfly is the caterpillar | The larval stage of a frog is the adult frog
